;; ADT-CARRIER-COLLAPSE-1. The latent trap, through a PAIR carrier.
;;
;; An OPAQUE carrier severs a cycle faithfully: `list[Tree]` emits `Lst`. A
;; TRANSPARENT carrier does not sever it, it COLLAPSES it. The field sort here is
;; `(Pair2 int int)`: the inner `Tree` becomes `int`, because the field sort is
;; computed alias-unaware, while a reflected constructor term over that payload
;; would carry `Tree`. Two sorts for one type is the `Elaborate fails` class.
;;
;; NOT a live defect, and the reason matters. Nothing reads the collapsed sort
;; because this function falls back, and it falls back on
;; `constraint-symbols-unbound` — the `FQ-FREEVAR-GUARD-1` guard, not a firewall.
;; The collapse is therefore unreachable BY ACCIDENT rather than by design, which
;; is exactly what this row was filed to record.
(export mk)
(type Tree (| Leaf) (| Node (int, Tree)))
(def-shell mk [n: int] -> Tree
  (pre (>= n 0))
  (post (= result (Node (pair n Leaf))))
  (Node (pair n Leaf)))
